In my teen years I read a comic book series called "Elementals."
Vortex (the "Air" superguy) had his eyes bitten out by a vampire in
one book, but could still read the position of his antagonist very
well by reading the air currents/displacement in the room. I just
assumed nethack air elementals did the same thing, and was actually
surprised when invisibility seemed to help.

That said, I dislike having invisibility taken from early game
characters as a means to help escape from the odd air elemental that
shows up there. Anybody that happens to is going to need all the help
they can get.






